From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:22:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: report data NSS in the firmware rx rate

The PHY rx info returned by the firmware carries NSTS, which for STBC
frames is twice the number of spatial streams, so station dumps showed
a doubled rx NSS and bitrate for STBC clients. Halve it for STBC, as
the RXV decoder does since "report data NSS for STBC frames in RX rate
decode", and reject an NSS cfg80211 can't handle. Also check the reply
is long enough before parsing it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 9b6f2fb1..67f4e594 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -4057,10 +4057,24 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_rx_rate(struct mt7915_phy *phy, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*res)) {
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	res = (struct mt7915_mcu_phy_rx_info *)skb->data;
 
 	rate->mcs = res->rate;
 	rate->nss = res->nsts + 1;
+	/* nsts counts space-time streams; report spatial streams, as
+	 * mt76_connac2_mac_fill_rx_rate() does for the RXV
+	 */
+	if (res->stbc && rate->nss > 1)
+		rate->nss >>= 1;
+	if (rate->nss > 8) {
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto out;
+	}
 
 	switch (res->mode) {
 	case MT_PHY_TYPE_CCK:
